I wish that more games existed like this. Every NPC drops every single item they have equipped. They will pick up equipment on the ground as well, so items are in constant circulation. I am just infatuated with how items work in this game, it's unlike any other game I've come across. Also, there is, luckily, no tutorial system. There is a well-rounded PvP system (determining who can and can not kill each other). However that's where the good parts end. The combat is abysmal and just a blind clickfest, no strategy/tactics are involved. The community is fractured and seemingly beyond repair; you would expect this from much larger MMOs. Also there is no sense of progrsesion. After about 4 hours in the game I got a sword that does +9 damage, and the best item in this game does +16, not much of a gap yet it would take you at least ten times as long to be able to access that item.
Using this as a base idea you could expand it into something beautiful:
) a much larger map, just one single server
) mobs that roam in herds and repopulate (so mobs can not respawn), so it is like applying item system to mobs
) no levels, skills, etc. Everything is dependent on your items alone
) no engravings, and items have a durability
) a crafting system that can combine lower items into strong ones
) while mobs can pick up items that are dropped on the ground, they are also able to craft their own
) player housing and guilds can be raided/thefted
) much harsher PvP restrictions so as to punish PKers more, but they will also have a ton of loot because of lack of engravings
) a combat system that requires a lot of forethought before and during combat
Anyways, the goal would be a very fast-paced high-risk-high-reward system, whereas this game has a low-risk no-reward system despite what it appears to be initially. Also death actually serves a purpose, as skills are no longer a thing and items can no longer be engraved.

